;
; The producer draws, and this puts what it drew on the panel.
;
; With DEVS:Monitors/AmigaVideo on the card, AROS renders through Denise --
; and nothing shows Denise by itself, on purpose. The panel keeps whatever
; the VideoCore last scanned out, so from the takeover onwards the desktop is
; invisible and there is nothing left to click. DeniseView therefore cannot be
; started by hand after the fact: it has to already be running.
;
; It holds the overlay plane for as long as it runs, above the desktop rather
; than instead of it, so this never returns. Run detaches it and the
; Startup-Sequence carries on.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-present] --- what the aperture holds now"
DeniseView >DEBUG: NOWINDOW

;
; The plane is installed from the descriptor as it reads at this instant --
; physical address, pitch and geometry. The pixels behind it are republished
; every frame, so the picture is live; the geometry is not. A guest that
; changes display mode after this needs the plane taken down and put up again,
; which is Ctrl-C and a second run.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-present] --- plane up (Ctrl-C in its shell takes it down)"
Run >NIL: <NIL: DeniseView SHOW
